    "source": "sharegpt",
    "why": "DENSITY TEST -- no longer a power test. The power hypothesis is dead (FINDINGS 6.2): T2 gained 26.7% with 1.4 W of headroom while T3 gained nothing with 36-57 W, and round one's power/gain correlation runs the wrong way (r=+0.717). Contention gates MPS, not watts. PREDICTION, registered before the run: T4 shows NO MPS effect. Scaling measured solo duty cycles to this scenario's per-tenant rates (llm2 2.4/s, embed 2.4/s, embed-small 1.6/s, rerank 1.6/s) gives a combined demand near 59% -- BELOW T3's 67%, which was a true null at p=0.90. dense4 is structurally low-contention because three of its four tenants are pooling models that sit near-idle; raising the rate cannot fix that without pushing llm2 past its own knee and conflating saturation with contention. WHAT IT DOES TEST, and nothing else in the matrix does: (a) HAMi admitting FOUR co-tenants on one card at 97.9% memory fill; (b) four vLLM engines profiling and capturing cudagraphs SIMULTANEOUSLY, which is exactly the init-peak collision 4.6a warns about and the densest memory moment in the study; (c) whether the per-tenant cost of sharing stays flat going from two tenants to four. Requirement 1 asks for number of models as a variable; this is its top end."
  },
